concepts.hero_flow:
1. User in Claude.ai: 'Run October payroll from my Team sheet.' The host's Google Drive connector reads three rows: Ada NGN 120,000 to GTBank; Wanjiru KES 6,000 to M-Pesa; Sam 40 USDC to sam.sol.
2. The agent calls core get_portfolio for the Solana wallet: 220 USDC, 0.05 SOL. If SOL is short, it calls core request_swap first.
3. The agent calls use_plugin(payrun.plan_run, wallet_id) {payer_address, chain:'solana:mainnet', payees[]}. In parallel, under 4 s, the backend:
   - resolves sam.sol via SNS;
   - runs Paycrest verify-account (ADA OBI matches, WANJIRU K matches);
   - screens wallets with GoPlus address_security;
   - checks for address-poisoning look-alikes against the payer's past counterparties;
   - quotes the rates.
   It returns run_id, per-payee lines (local amount, USDC, rate, spread), a total of 175.40 USDC, 0.004 SOL rent for new token accounts, and '1 approval'. No approval.
4. User: 'Approve payroll.' The agent calls payrun.propose_run {run_id}. The backend creates 2 Paycrest orders on Solana (source.refundAddress = payer) and compiles ONE v0 transaction containing:
   - createAssociatedTokenAccountIdempotent for any missing recipient token account;
   - 3x SPL TransferChecked of USDC (EPjFWdd5AufqSSqeM2qN1xzybapC8G4wEGGkZwyTDt1v) to sam.sol and the two providerAccount.receiveAddresses;
   - Memo 'payrun:<run_id>'.
   The payer is the only signer and fee payer, the size is about 650 B, and the blockhash is a placeholder. The tool returns a solana proposal.
5. PayBox simulates and opens the window. APPROVAL 1: passkey. PayBox signs, broadcasts and confirms.
6. The agent calls payrun.verify_run {run_id, signature}. The backend reads pre/post token balances (Alchemy Solana RPC) and confirms each credit is exact. It polls Paycrest /v2/sender/orders/:id until settled, then returns signed payslips (payee, local amount, rate, Solana tx, LP settlement tx). Any expired fiat leg has already been refunded to the payer and is flagged for a one-tap re-run.

Visible outcome: three notifications from one signature (GTBank SMS, M-Pesa SMS, Phantom +40 USDC).

Base variant: payrun.ensure_allowance returns a one-time EVM approve to a 25-line PayrunBatch contract that can only transferFrom msg.sender. After that, payrun.propose_run_base is one EVM call, so every run costs one approval.
